  "sections": {
    "guide": {
      "hero_eyebrow": "A Guide to Your",
      "hero_title": "Tre Cookware",
      "hero_p1": "The Essential Collection is our quiet promise: to care for your kitchen, your meals, and the moments that matter most, with tools built to endure and made to nurture.",
      "hero_p2": "Your cookware is crafted with pure, safe, high quality materials, free from harmful additives or coatings.",
      "index_title": "Index",
      "ch1_title": "Only What's Essential",
      "ch2_title": "Materials",
      "ch3_title": "Design",
      "ch4_title": "Cleaning and Care",
      "ch5_title": "How to Use Your Cookware",
      "ch6_title": "Common Concerns",
      "ch7_title": "Tre Warranty",
      "one": "One",
      "two": "Two",
      "three": "Three",
      "four": "Four",
      "five": "Five",
      "six": "Six",
      "seven": "Seven",
      "essential_sub": "The Essential Collection.",
      "essential_p1": "The foundation of every kitchen begins with the right tools. The Essential Collection is a carefully chosen set of cookware, timeless pieces crafted from premium stainless steel and designed to meet the rhythm of everyday cooking.",
      "essential_p2": "Each piece balances versatility with efficiency, giving you the core sizes and functions you'll reach for again and again. Thoughtfully curated and beautifully made, this is the heart of your kitchen.",
      "size_20": "20cm",
      "size_26": "26cm",
      "size_28": "28cm",
      "size_16": "16cm",
      "piece_frying_pan": "Frying Pan",
      "piece_sauce_pan": "Sauce Pan",
      "piece_saute_pan": "Sauté Pan",
      "piece_stockpot_small": "Stockpot",
      "piece_stockpot_large": "Stockpot",
      "piece_steamer": "Steamer",
      "uncoated_sub": "Uncoated Stainless Steel.",
      "uncoated_p1": "Cooking with uncoated stainless steel offers a level of purity and peace of mind that coated alternatives, even those labeled “non-toxic”, simply can't match.",
      "uncoated_p2": "With no synthetic layers or chemical treatments, uncoated steel is naturally inert, meaning it won't break down, leach, or react with your food, even at high temperatures.",
      "uncoated_p3": "Unlike coated pans, which can degrade over time and may contain binders or stabilizers with unknown long-term effects, stainless steel remains stable and reliable for life.",
      "uncoated_p4": "It's a healthier choice, no coatings to chip, no hidden risks, just clean, safe cooking, every single time.",
      "five_ply_sub": "Five Ply Construction",
      "five_ply_intro": "The multi-layered structure includes:",
      "layer_interior_t": "18/10 Stainless Steel Interior",
      "layer_interior_d": "A non-reactive, non-corrosive, low-maintenance finish that resists sticking and simplifies cleanup.",
      "layer_aluminum_t": "3 Aluminum Layers",
      "layer_aluminum_d": "Ensures rapid, even heat diffusion across the surface with precise thermal responsiveness for enhanced temperature control.",
      "layer_exterior_t": "403 Stainless Steel Exterior",
      "layer_exterior_d": "A durable, polished surface, built to look elegant and withstand daily use.",
      "layer_lid_t": "1.0mm Lid",
      "layer_lid_d": "Thick stainless steel 1.0 mm lid engineered to seal in moisture and flavor during cooking.",
      "layer_handles_t": "Handles",
      "layer_handles_d": "Cast handle built to last for decades.",
      "design_sealed_t": "Complete Sealed Rims Technology",
      "design_sealed_d": "Although hand washing is the gold standard when it comes to caring for your beloved cookware, sealed rims are what make cookware truly dishwasher-safe.",
      "design_lids_t": "Universal Lid Compatibility",
      "design_lids_d": "Thoughtfully designed lids fit multiple TRE pieces, between sauté pans, frypans and stockpots.",
      "design_handle_t": "Comfortable Handle",
      "design_handle_d": "Its thoughtful design ensures easy maneuverability, allowing you to stir, pour, and serve with confidence.",
      "design_edges_t": "Sleek, Flared Edges",
      "design_edges_d": "For effortless flipping and pouring.",
      "care_1_t": "Deglaze and Let it Cool",
      "care_1_d": "Right after cooking, while the pan is still hot, add a small amount of water to deglaze the pan of any stuck or burnt food. This will help make cleaning so much easier. Allow the pan to cool naturally before washing.",
      "care_2_t": "Wash",
      "care_2_d1": "Use dish soap and a non abrasive sponge or brush to clean the pan.",
      "care_2_d2": "You can use the dishwasher. Your cookware is dishwasher safe thanks to its sealed rims. That being said, hand washing is always best.",
      "care_3_t": "Dry",
      "care_3_d": "Wipe dry with a microfiber towel to reveal the brilliant shine of polished steel.",
      "care_4_t": "Polish",
      "care_4_d": "For cookware stained and dulled from regular use, restore shine with vinegar, baking soda, or TRE Treatment Powder for those resistant stains. Apply TRE treatment only occasionally as a refresh.",
      "use_lede": "Cooking with stainless steel has a learning curve, but once you master the heat, the results are worth it.",
      "use_1_t": "1. Warm it Up First",
      "use_1_d1": "Start with low to medium heat. A few water drops should glide when it's ready.",
      "use_1_d2": "TRE cookware retains heat beautifully — gentle to medium heat is all you need.",
      "use_2_t": "2. Add Oil After Heating",
      "use_2_d": "This creates a natural barrier to help prevent sticking.",
      "use_3_t": "3. Let Food Release Naturally",
      "use_3_d": "Food will release on its own when it's ready, no need to force it.",
      "use_4_t": "4. Use What You Love",
      "use_4_d": "Metal, wood, or silicone utensils, your cookware can handle it.",
      "concern_1_t": "Discoloration and spots",
      "concern_1_d1": "Overheating an empty pan or leaving it unattended on a flame can cause discoloration. This is a natural metal reaction and won't affect performance or safety. If you ever miss the shine, use TRE powder to restore the pan's original look.",
      "concern_1_d2": "White spots or stains are often caused by minerals in water. A mixture of vinegar and water can help dissolve them.",
      "concern_2_t": "Food sticking",
      "concern_2_d": "Try preheating a bit longer and adding oil after the pan is hot. Let food release naturally, it will lift when it's ready.",
      "concern_3_t": "Handles getting hot",
      "concern_3_d": "TRE handles are stainless steel too, always use a mitt when cooking for longer periods or using the oven.",
      "warranty_p1": "TRE cookware makes healthy eating kind to your body and your budget.",
      "warranty_p2": "Backed by a lifetime warranty against manufacturing or craftsmanship issues.",
      "warranty_claims": "Warranty claims:",
      "closing_title": "Good tools cultivate good habits.",
      "closing_p1": "Thank you for choosing TRE to be part of your kitchen. We look forward to seeing how you create delicious meals, one thoughtful dish at a time. Don't forget to share your culinary journey with us.",
      "closing_p2": "Bring your recipe to the table and inspire fellow home-chefs in the TRE community.",
      "alt_hero": "TRE stainless steel cookware set on a range",
      "alt_closeup": "Close-up of an uncoated stainless steel pan",
      "alt_five_ply": "Cutaway diagram of the five ply construction: 403 stainless steel exterior, three aluminum layers, and an 18/10 stainless steel interior",
      "alt_saucepan": "TRE stainless steel sauce pan with lid",
      "alt_frypan": "TRE stainless steel frying pan",
